{"id":"u-316573c3-04ee-48e3-bb70-4854390e8c25","src":"community","title":"Overcoming Gravity: 4-Day Upper / Lower Split","author":"Eduardo G.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/xD4LDe-overcoming-gravity-4-day-upper-lower-split","desc":"Adapted from Steven Low's Overcoming Gravity (2nd Edition), an Upper / Lower split across 4 training days per week provides an ideal balance of upper-body volume, systemic recovery, and joint/tendon preservation for intermediate calisthenics practitioners. I made it specially for me, a 44 year old, using the book, experience and Gemini (full disclosure).\n\nWhy Upper / Lower?\nUnlike a Push/Pull split (which trains upper-body musculature and shoulder girdles across 4 consecutive or near-consecutive sessions), an Upper / Lower routine completely rests the upper-body connective tissue (rotator cuff, bicep tendons, medial/lateral epicondyles) on Lower days. This allows higher upper-body volume per session while providing 72–96 hours of recovery between upper-body sessions.\n\nWeekly Schedule\n\nMonday: Day 1 – Upper Body A Upper\nTuesday: Day 2 – Lower Body & Core A Lower\nWednesday: Complete Rest / Active Recovery Mobility\nThursday: Day 3 – Upper Body B Upper\nFriday: Day 4 – Lower Body & Core B Lower\nSaturday & Sunday: Rest / Light Cardio / Passive Recovery\n\nCore Overcoming Gravity Guidelines\n\nVolume: Upper sessions feature 4 primary movements: 2 Push (1 Horizontal, 1 Vertical) and 2 Pull (1 Horizontal, 1 Vertical) with 3 working sets each (12 total sets per session; 24 upper-body sets weekly). Lower sessions feature 2 primary leg exercises (quad-dominant, hip/hamstring-dominant), 1 calf/ankle drill, and 2 targeted core/compression exercises.\n\nIntensity Bracket: Primary strength & hypertrophy range: 5–8 repetitions (or 10–15s for isometric static holds). Accessory work stays in the 8–12 repetition range.\n\nRest Intervals: 3 minutes between direct sets. Paired sets can be used between antagonistic movements (e.g., Pull-up → rest 90s → Dip → rest 90s → repeat) to maintain high neural output while economizing time.\n\nTempo (10X0): 1 second controlled eccentric (lowering), 0 second pause at bottom, eXplosive concentric, 0 second pause at top (unless a static pause is prescribed).\n\nProgression: Progress to the next leverage progression only after achieving all 3 sets at the top rep target with clean, controlled form.\nPre-Workout Warm-Up & Skill Work (All Days)\n\nPre-workout:\n\n1. Warmup (10 min)\nFor this I do the Reddit Recommended Routine Warm up:\nhttps://www.reddit.com/r/bodyweightfitness/wiki/kb/recommended_routine/\n\n3. Cardio (5 min)\nHollow Body Hold: 2 × 30–45s (lower back pushed flat into floor).\nArch Body (Superman) Hold: 2 × 30–45s (glutes and posterior chain active).\n\n3. Skill Work — Non-Fatiguing (Upper Days Only, 5–10 min)\nDepends on the level. I do these:\nHandstand: 3–4 sets of 20–30s. Push through shoulders into elevation; do not train to muscular failure.\nRings Support Hold (RTO): 3 sets × 15–20s. Lock elbows completely, turn rings out (45°–90°), depress scapulae.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Bodyweight Fitness"],"equipment":["At Home"],"minutes":60,"joins":0,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-09-27T22:44:26.313Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Upper Body","Day 2: Lower Body & Core A (Un","Day 3: Upper Body B (Leverage","Day 4"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Yuri'S Shoulder Band Warmup","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":3}]},{"n":"Squat Sky Reaches","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":30,"rpe":5}]},{"n":"GMB Wrist Prep","sets":[{"lo":30,"hi":60,"rpe":5}]},{"n":"Strict Pull-Up","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ring Dip","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"One Arm Ring Rows","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":18,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pseudo Planche Push-Up","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ring Face Pulls With External Rotation","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pistol Squat","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Nordic Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single-Leg Calf Raises","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Reverse Hyperextension","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Tuck Front Lever Rows","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Elevated Pike Push-Ups","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ring L-Sit Pull-Up","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Decline Ring Push-Ups","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ring Pelican / Bicep Curls Superset W/ Tricep Extensions","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Shrimp Squats","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Glute Bridge (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tibialis Wall Raises","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":20,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ring Ab Rollouts","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Side Plank Rotations","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Yuri'S Shoulder Band Warmup","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":3}]},{"n":"Squat Sky Reaches","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":30,"rpe":5}]},{"n":"GMB Wrist Prep","sets":[{"lo":30,"hi":60,"rpe":5}]},{"n":"Strict Pull-Up","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ring Dip","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"One Arm Ring Rows","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":18,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pseudo Planche Push-Up","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ring Face Pulls With External Rotation","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Pistol Squat","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Nordic Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"lo":5,"hi":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single-Leg Calf Raises","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Reverse Hyperextension","sets":[{"lo":12,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Tuck Front Lever Rows","sets":[{"lo":4,"hi":6,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Elevated Pike Push-U